@startuml
title F03 - Kit provisioning and installation verification
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Installer" as Installer
boundary "A01\nApp onboarding" as A01
control "B06\nFleet/config" as B06
control "S03\nFirmware security/update" as S03
control "H07\nHub lifecycle/config" as H07
control "N04\nNode lifecycle" as N04
control "T02\nHardware-in-loop tools" as T02
Installer -> A01: Scan/enter one hub and four unique node identities
A01 -> B06: Claim devices for the authorized home
B06 -> S03: Validate board identity, credential reference and update policy
B06 -> H07: Publish versioned hub configuration
H07 -> N04: Open bounded service window and apply node configurations
N04 -> B06: Report applied version and device binding
T02 -> H07: Observe hub controls, input sources, RF and delivery test evidence
T02 -> A01: Return pass/fail installation gate with missing checks
note over A01,Installer: Unobserved hardware checks remain failed; the tool never invents a board result.
note over Installer,T02: Outcome - The kit is eligible only when identity, configuration, every enabled input and a real TEST delivery are evidenced.
@enduml
